# Sufi Map — Cursor AI Rules

This is the **Sufi Map** project. Read `AGENTS.md` and `PROJECT_STATE.md` before making any changes.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui components (always use `shadcn` MCP to find/install — never hand-write what shadcn provides)
- Supabase (Postgres + PostGIS, Auth, Storage) — use `supabase` MCP for migrations
- MapLibre GL JS with CARTO Voyager vector tiles
- next-intl: en / ml / ar with full RTL support

## Sahn Design Tokens (strict — never deviate)
| Token | Value | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| `background` | `#FAF9F4` | Warm parchment canvas |
| `card` | `#FFFFFF` | White surface |
| `foreground` | `#121512` | Deep charcoal ink |
| `muted-foreground` | `#5D675F` | Soft stone grey |
| `primary` | `#1F5C3A` | Deep sanctuary green |
| `border` | `#E4E2D8` | Warm grey border |

## Design Rules
- **Border radius**: always `rounded-[14px]` (0.875rem). Never `rounded-lg` alone.
- **Fonts**: `font-serif` (Playfair Display) for headings, `font-sans` (Inter) for body, `font-arabic` (Amiri) for Arabic with `dir="rtl"`.
- **Buttons**: `active:scale-[0.98] transition-all duration-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`
- **Cards**: `card-lift` utility (defined in globals.css) — adds `hover:-translate-y-2 shadow-lift`
- **Shadows**: use `shadow-float` (deep) or `shadow-lift` (light) CSS utilities
- **Quote**: use `RotatingQuote` component, never inline raw quote JSX

## Ethical Rules
- Never fabricate historical facts, dates, or stories
- Seed/sample data must be explicitly marked `[SAMPLE]`
- Living Sufi profiles: only public gathering places; require `consent_status = 'granted'`
- RLS mandatory on every Supabase table

## Token Efficiency
- DRY — reuse existing components
- No new dependencies unless absolutely necessary
- Always run `npm run build` and confirm zero TypeScript errors before finishing
